# General Instructions
- Prioritize high performance, code readability, and simplicity.
- Avoid over-engineering, unnecessary abstractions, or overly complex architecture for simple features.
- Write easy-to-debug code with clear naming and straightforward patterns.
- Do not introduce boilerplate or multi-layered wrappers unless explicitly requested or strictly necessary for scale.

# Code Style & Quality
- Keep functions small, focused, and single-purpose.
- Prefer explicit and clear code over overly clever or concise solutions.
- Keep state management and structure lightweight.